Catalog number : I00048
Uniform title: Viśeṣāntyeṣṭi
Manuscript : IFP manuscript bundle RE30586
Description: RE30586 This manuscript contains the procedural instructions (pūjā methods) for the final rites (funeral ceremonies) as detailed in the Śivāgamas. These rites are to be performed for Śivāchāryas (priests consecrated for the worship of Śiva) and Śivanadiyars (devotees of Śiva) who have undergone Śaivadīkṣā (initiation) at different levels: (1) Samayam (Śāmayān), (2) Viśēṣam (Putrakan), (3) Nirvāṇam (Sādhakan) (4) Āchāriyābhiṣēkam (Āchāriyan) Viśēṣadīkṣā is defined as the process for Śivanadiyars to gain liberation from their malabāṣakarmā māyai (impurities, bondage, and delusion). This is achieved through the descent of the Lord (Vāgīśvarī Vāgīśvarar) to take birth in their garbhanāḍi (core energy channel), followed by the devotee’s daily worship of Śivaperumān and the subsequent attainment of Śivajñāna (divine knowledge of Śiva). The codex covers the final rites procedures up to the Viśēṣam level of initiation. It provides clear and explicit descriptions of: (1) The method of performing the pūjā at the designated location (iḍamāka) in uncircumscribed order. (2) The application of the Śakti Jāla Prayōgam (the utilization/application of the net of power/energy).Observations - The manuscript does not specify the particular Āgama upon which these procedures are based. A different subject matter is discussed on page 37b of this codex. The condition of the bundle is good. The size of the manuscript is 3.4 cm x 26.5 cm, and there are 6 lines in each folio.
